statement:
A bug stands at position `0` of a number line and wants to land on position `x`. Every move is one of two jumps: exactly `a` units to the right, or exactly `b` units to the left. The rules are:

- two left jumps may never come directly one after the other;
- the bug may never land on a negative position or on any position listed in `forbidden` (it only has to avoid landing there, not flying over it);
- it is allowed to land to the right of `x` and come back later.

Return the smallest number of jumps after which the bug stands on `x`, or `-1` if no sequence of jumps ever lands it there.

validator:
function validate([forbidden, a, b, x]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(forbidden) || forbidden.length < 1 || forbidden.length > 1000) return 'forbidden needs 1 to 1000 positions.';
  if (forbidden.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < 1 || v > 2000)) return 'Each forbidden position is between 1 and 2000.';
  if (new Set(forbidden).size !== forbidden.length) return 'forbidden positions must be distinct.';
  if (!Number.isInteger(a) || a < 1 || a > 2000) return 'a is between 1 and 2000.';
  if (!Number.isInteger(b) || b < 1 || b > 2000) return 'b is between 1 and 2000.';
  if (!Number.isInteger(x) || x < 0 || x > 2000) return 'x is between 0 and 2000.';
  if (forbidden.includes(x)) return 'x cannot be a forbidden position.';
  return null;
}

